</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>In-depth Analysis</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Experiments: Creativity and Discovery ‣ Shared Nature, Unique Nurture: PRISM for Pluralistic Reasoning via In-context Structure Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> demonstrated the overall effectiveness of PRISM across benchmarks, this section zooms in to dissect the system’s operational mechanisms and boundary conditions. Specifically, we isolate the impact of the Epistemic Graph, model scale, the breadth of exploration seeds, and lexical diversity to provide insight into the critical design trade-offs governing the system’s effectiveness.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S5.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation Study: Contribution of the Epistemic Graph structure vs. Flat RAG.</span></figcaption>
